 "transport": "JSON, one compact object: keys in field-number order after the schema, a zero, empty or false field without presence left out. The iPhone app sends a RouteRequest to POST /api/chat/route/v1 and reads the RouteDecision back; a connected computer's resident service answers DescribeStation (an environment RPC) with a StationReport, which the app reads through GET /api/chat/environment/station/v1.",
 "about": "Each body goes through the generated JSON mapper and comes back byte for byte; each RouteRequest also reads through wire.coax's rtr_request_read and is written back by rtr_request_write to the same bytes (docs/router/README.md). Each StationReport also reads through rtr_report_read and is written back by rtr_report_write, and each DescribeStation through rtr_describe_read and rtr_describe_write, to the same bytes.",
